---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { email, site } from '../config';
import { hasArt, ownArt } from '../lib/art';
---

<DocLayout picture={ownArt('page-legal-terms', 'page-legal')}
  banner={hasArt('page-legal-terms')}
  title="Terms and EULA"
  h1="Stillroom Vault terms and licence agreement"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description="The end-user licence agreement for Stillroom Vault: what a licence covers, your responsibility for your password and recovery key, and the limits of our liability."
  lead="The short version: one licence is for one person, on all of their own Macs. Your vault is yours alone, so a forgotten password and lost recovery key can’t be undone by anyone, us included."
  updated="26 October 2026"
  draft
  legal
>
    <h2 id="who">1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Stillroom Vault (“Stillroom”, “the app”) is made and owned by {site.owners.join(' and ')}, and sold by {site.seller},
      an individual based in {site.sellerCountry} (“we”, “us”). These terms are an agreement between you and us about using the app and any
      licence key you buy. Write to <a href={`mailto:${email.legal}`}>{email.legal}</a> with any question about them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our order process is conducted by our online reseller Paddle.com. Paddle.com is the Merchant of Record for all our
      orders. Paddle provides all customer service inquiries and handles returns. When you buy, Paddle’s
      <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/checkout-buyer-terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">buyer terms</a> apply to the purchase itself. For help with
      the app, write to <a href={`mailto:${email.support}`}>{email.support}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="licence">2. Your licence</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Free:</strong> you may use the app, with every feature, for up to 25 items, for as long as you like.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Stillroom Vault ($39):</strong> one person may use the app without the item limit on every Mac they own
        or personally use.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Family ($129):</strong> up to five people you choose, each on every Mac they own or personally use.</li>
      <li><strong>Teams:</strong> the number of people agreed with us in writing.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      A licence includes every 1.x update. A later major version (2.0) may be a paid upgrade; the version you bought keeps
      working. We don’t promise to make updates, but every update to 1.x is included when we do.
    </p>
    <p>
      Please don’t share, publish or resell your licence key. It’s checked on your Mac, offline, and carries the email
      address you bought with.
    </p>
    <p>
      The app’s source code is separately available under the <a href="/license/">Functional Source License 1.1
      (FSL-1.1-ALv2)</a>, and the vault reader in <code>tools/</code> under the MIT licence. Those licences govern the
      source code; these terms govern copies of the app we distribute and the licence keys we sell.
    </p>

    <h2 id="your-vault">3. Your vault is your responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      Stillroom has no server and no account, and we never have a copy of your files, your password, your recovery key
      or your emergency kit. That’s the point of it, and it means:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>If you forget your password and lose your recovery key and enough kit pieces, nobody can open your vault,
        not even us.</strong> We can’t reset it, recover it or get your files back.
      </li>
      <li>
        Keeping backups is up to you. The app makes encrypted backups and can export everything as ordinary files; please
        use them.
      </li>
      <li>
        The app has limits, documented plainly in our <a href="/security/">security rules</a>: for example, it doesn’t
        protect against a weak password or against malware with administrator rights while the vault is open, and the
        decoy is protection against thieves and abusers, not police.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="warranty">4. No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      We build Stillroom carefully and test it, but we provide it “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any
      kind, to the fullest extent the law allows. We don’t promise that it will be free of errors, or that it will keep
      your data safe from every risk.
    </p>

    <h2 id="liability">5. Limits of our liability</h2>
    <p>To the fullest extent the law allows:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        we are not liable for lost or damaged data, including data you can’t open because a password, recovery key or kit
        was forgotten or lost;
      </li>
      <li>we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special or consequential losses, or lost profits;</li>
      <li>our total liability to you for anything to do with Stillroom is limited to what you paid for your licence.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Nothing in these terms limits liability that can’t be limited by law, such as for fraud, or takes away rights you
      have as a consumer under the law of the country you live in.
    </p>

    <h2 id="refunds">6. Refunds</h2>
    <p>You can get a full refund within 14 days of buying, for any reason. See the <a href="/refunds/">refund policy</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="law">7. Using it lawfully</h2>
    <p>
      Stillroom uses strong encryption. You’re responsible for following the laws that apply where you use it, including
      rules about encryption and about exporting it. Don’t use or send Stillroom anywhere, or to anyone, that export or
      sanctions laws forbid.
    </p>

    <h2 id="ending">8. Ending this agreement</h2>
    <p>
      If you break these terms, your licence to use Stillroom beyond the free tier ends. Opening, exporting and backing up
      your vault always keep working, licensed or not: we never hold your files hostage.
    </p>

    <h2 id="general">9. General</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Kosovo, and disputes go to the courts of Prishtina, without
      taking away any protection the law of your own country gives you as a consumer, including the right to go to your
      own courts. These terms and Paddle’s buyer terms are the whole agreement about Stillroom. If a court finds part of
      them unenforceable, the rest still applies. You may not transfer your licence without our agreement in writing.
    </p>
    <p>
      If we change these terms, we’ll post the new version here with its date; the terms you accepted when you bought keep
      applying to that purchase.
    </p>
</DocLayout>
